{"id": "idaho-2", "headline": "Idaho health officials seek 13% raise for disability caregivers", "source": "Idaho Capital Sun", "url": "https://idahocapitalsun.com/2026/11/19/idaho-officials-request-raise-for-disability-caregivers-and-restoring-cuts-to-mental-health-services/", "published": "2026-11-19", "url_verified": true, "pages": ["Idaho's Department of Health and Welfare wants to raise pay for disability caregivers by 13% next year, according to its budget proposal sent to the governor in September. The rate for personal care service workers would rise from 24.44 dollars to 27.64 dollars an hour. That could lift Idaho out of its place as the lowest paying state in the Northwest for the industry for the first time in years. Idaho has long faced a shortage of disability caregivers. The request is a rare departure from the governor's office's instruction for agencies to keep submitting barebones budgets after deep cuts in the 2026 legislative session.", "Medicaid Administrator Sasha O'Connell said the department asked after learning that few caregiving agencies can take new patients. That research was required by federal regulators as part of the state's recent cuts to doctor pay rates. The proposal also seeks to restore some mental health service cuts. Source: Idaho Capital Sun."], "qr": {"n": 45, "rows": ["111111101100111001001111001011110100101111111", "100000100011100010110101110011011101001000001", "101110100111100001100011101101011101001011101", "101110100100011001110000011110011101101011101", "101110100010000100011111111000111011101011101", "100000100000000111001000101101001000001000001", "111111101010101010101010101010101010101111111", "000000001101001101101000101010100000100000000", "110110100010110011111111110010110010001000001", "010110011001011010011010011100110111111110010", "001101100101011000110010100010010111100100111", "110001000000001010110110110000101100110000100", "111100100110001100110100101110001101000010001", "110001000110010100011110001110